# The Planetary Council's window (CouncWin, see src/ui/councwin.c): the keys and the button no one has. A key that is not Return or Escape
# does nothing. Return, before the player has voted, makes the AIs vote that have not (a poke empties faction 2's vote; the seat shows it
# again). The button -2 (the window's own handler, called by hand) does the same while no human has voted, and nothing after. Then the
# player's own Yea decides the vote; the button -2 then ends the window (the vote is decided), which carries the proposal out (+500
# energy credits to every faction: the tables are in the state). A second window, opened in the scenario editor's debugging mode (a poke
# sets the bits), ends on Return without a vote (the proposal is not carried out), and a third on the button -2. The state regions are as in
# councwin_vote.scene.
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
